       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error. Ibuprofen 4000 mg four times daily comes to 16,000 mg/day. That is 5 times the usual maximum for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under supervision, or 1,200 mg/day for OTC use. A single 4000 mg dose is also far above the usual 400\u2013800 mg per dose. It could cause serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg** PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg** PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg** PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If 4000 mg per dose is what you intend, please confirm that explicitly and I'll add a note to the order."
