      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen 4000 mg per dose is about 57 mg/kg for a 70 kg patient, and four doses a day is 16 g. Those amounts are in the range where toxicity is expected, including GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, and CNS effects. I know of no indication that calls for this dose, and I can't enter an order I expect to seriously harm the patient.\n\nYou have a few options:\n- **Enter a different dose.** I can enter 400 mg QID, 800 mg TID, or 800 mg QID (the 3,200 mg/day maximum) right away.\n- **Order it outside my tools.** If you have a rationale I'm not aware of, you can order it directly in the EHR. Pharmacy will probably need to verify it.\n- **Consider another drug.** If the goal is stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect, I can enter a different agent or a multimodal regimen at standard doses.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
